feat(v2): wire JK-hybrid TUI dashboard into the Fastify route

Replaces the v1 MongoDB-flavored dashboard at src/server/routes/
dashboardHtml.ts with the JK-hybrid layout (cream paper, ink-bordered,
K-palette colored, 3-pane TUI structure). Live-wired to /state and
/events SSE.

What the new dashboard does:
- /atlas-stats on boot + every 15s: hydrates the storage driver
  ("sqlite-vec"), tools count, violations count, MCP/fixture/catalog
  counts in the left nav.
- /state on boot: populates the ranking table (alphabetical browse
  mode by default), domain counts in the nav, domain-tab counters.
  Picks the highest-reliability active tool as the initial selection.
- /events SSE: pushes structured rows into the LIVE FEED in the right
  pane (DSCV/CALL/CB/PUSH/EVAL chips). Capped to 20.
- discover_ran event switches the table to ranking mode (top-1 yellow
  row + orange arrow), updates the pane head with the query + total_ms.
- tool_invoked event flashes the matching row orange for 1s.
- violation_logged increments the red violations counter in the top
  bar + nav.
- Domain tab click filters the browse view; left-nav domain rows are
  also clickable and proxy to the matching tab.
- Row click in the table updates the right-pane DETAIL with the
  selected tool's blurb, reliability bar, p95, cost, status, stub.

Required infra fix:
- src/storage/index.ts factory was still throwing 'SqliteStorage not
  yet implemented' from the Step 4 placeholder. Now lazy-imports
  SqliteStorage and resolves TWOCHAIN_DB_PATH (default
  ~/.2chain/db.sqlite).
- Default STORAGE_DRIVER changed from 'mongodb' to 'sqlite' so
  `npm run dev:v2` works out of the box.

Verified locally on PORT=3031: /health reports storage=sqlite +
embedder=ollama:nomic-embed-text, /atlas-stats returns 430 tools /
199 eval_runs / 1 violation, dashboard HTML serves with the new
<title>2chain · tool registry</title>.

91 tests pass. lint:no-mongodb clean. typecheck clean.

